1
00:05:57,142 --> 00:06:03,142
Some men are too noble to live among aristocracy.

2
00:11:54,285 --> 00:12:00,285
Vatel is a history, drama, romance film directed by Roland Joffé.

3
00:17:51,428 --> 00:17:57,428
In 1671, with war brewing with Holland, a penniless prince invites Louis
XIV to three days of festivities at a chateau in Chantilly.

4
00:23:48,571 --> 00:23:54,571
The prince wants a commission as a general, so the
extravagances are to impress the king.

5
00:29:45,714 --> 00:29:51,714
In charge of all is the steward, Vatel, a man of honor, talent, and low birth.

6
00:35:42,857 --> 00:35:48,857
The prince is craven in his longing for stature: no task is too
menial or dishonorable for him to give Vatel.

7
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:46,000
While Vatel tries to sustain dignity, he finds himself attracted
to Anne de Montausier, the king's newest mistress.

8
00:47:37,142 --> 00:47:43,142
In Vatel, she finds someone who's authentic, living out his
principles within the casual cruelties of court politics.

9
00:53:34,285 --> 00:53:40,285
Can the two of them escape unscathed?

10
00:59:31,428 --> 00:59:37,428
Francois Vatel, played by Gérard Depardieu.

11
01:05:28,571 --> 01:05:34,571
Anne de Montausier, played by Uma Thurman.

12
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
Marquis de Lauzun, played by Tim Roth.

13
01:17:22,857 --> 01:17:28,857
Gourville, played by Timothy Spall.

14
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
Prince de Conde, played by Julian Glover.

15
01:29:17,142 --> 01:29:23,142
Louis XIV, played by Julian Sands.

16
01:35:14,285 --> 01:35:20,285
Vatel is a 2000 historical drama film directed by Roland Joffé, written by Jeanne Labrune and translated by Tom
Stoppard, and starring Gérard Depardieu, Uma Thurman, Tim Roth, Timothy Spall, Julian Glover and Julian Sands.

17
01:41:11,428 --> 01:41:17,428
The film, based on the life of 17th-century French chef François Vatel,
was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Art Direction.

18
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
The film opened the 2000 Cannes Film Festival.

19
01:53:05,714 --> 01:53:11,714
The film explores themes of france, prince, chef, 17th century, louis xiv.

20
01:59:02,857 --> 01:59:08,857
The tone is emotional.
